  "instruction_steps": [
    {
      "step_number": 1,
      "instruction": "First, make the curry paste. Use a pestle and mortar to pound together the dried and fresh chillies, shrimp paste, garlic, galangal, lemongrass, lime zest, white pepper, coriander, cumin, nutmeg and peanuts, plus 1 tsp salt. You should have a rough paste. Alternatively, add all the ingredients to a food processor along with 2-3 tbsp of coconut milk and pulse until you have a paste. Store in a lidded jar in the fridge. Will keep for up to two weeks.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "8627a25b-af63-522d-ae0f-cb7ccf7a47e2",
        "2707771b-816f-54da-bbea-98b468907eec",
        "b8bd4f3d-d0e0-54ba-a156-27b37cacdaba",
        "f588b383-85da-5a34-a20a-f59e0bf855b9",
        "a61b5866-faf4-51aa-bdd2-36931ac0ba89",
        "618ebb79-8356-59a5-9c45-2e39b8300ddd",
        "9ae0da43-ecd5-509c-a20a-c28a664af8b3",
        "455eaf99-093c-50e0-830a-9864a4034795",
        "c380fa01-b4c8-5ce0-aedb-ab258af1e755",
        "62c9149a-0227-52d7-9dd1-f90872fbc6a0",
        "c8e8b7f8-6c50-5d22-b9cf-016b5f1ef21b",
        "445864bd-9b42-5336-8a49-32a3deb8009b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 2,
      "instruction": "Add 2-3 tbsp of the thick part of the coconut milk into a saucepan over a medium-high heat. When the coconut milk starts bubbling, add 1-2 tbsp of the curry paste and stir well for about 1 min, until fragrant.",
      "timer_seconds": 60,
      "ingredients_used": [
        "8627a25b-af63-522d-ae0f-cb7ccf7a47e2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 3,
      "instruction": "Stir in the chicken and let it cook for about 3-4 mins until beginning to brown all over. Follow with the French beans and stir well.",
      "timer_seconds": 240,
      "ingredients_used": [
        "e45372d0-3569-556a-a2c6-6ba7c5f91090"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 4,
      "instruction": "Season with the fish sauce and sugar, then add the rest of coconut milk. Mix well, add half the makrut lime leaves and simmer for 3-5 mins until the chicken is cooked through. Taste and add more sugar or fish sauce if necessary – it should be salty and nutty, and the sweetness should come through. Add the Thai basil leaves, give it a quick mix and take off the heat. Serve with steamed jasmine rice, garnished with the sliced chilli and the rest of the makrut lime leaves.",
      "timer_seconds": 300,
      "ingredients_used": [
        "8627a25b-af63-522d-ae0f-cb7ccf7a47e2",
        "7f8bed8a-0c63-5875-a15c-32939907be77",
